{
  "schemaVersion": 2,
  "bookCode": "RV10",
  "bookSlug": "rig-veda-book-10",
  "n": 190,
  "paragraphs": [
    {
      "n": 1,
      "refId": "RV10-190:1",
      "text": "translated by"
    },
    {
      "n": 2,
      "refId": "RV10-190:2",
      "text": "1. FROM Fervour kindled to its height Eternal Law and Truth were born:",
      "original": "ऋतं च सत्यं चाभीद्धात्तपसोऽध्यजायत ।",
      "translit": "ṛtaṃ ca satyaṃ cābhīddhāttapaso'dhyajāyata |"
    },
    {
      "n": 3,
      "refId": "RV10-190:3",
      "text": "Thence was the Night produced, and thence the billowy flood of sea arose.",
      "original": "ततो रात्र्यजायत ततः समुद्रो अर्णवः",
      "translit": "tato rātryajāyata tataḥ samudro arṇavaḥ"
    },
    {
      "n": 4,
      "refId": "RV10-190:4",
      "text": "2. From that same billowy flood of sea the Year was afterwards produced,",
      "original": "समुद्रादर्णवादधि संवत्सरो अजायत ।",
      "translit": "samudrādarṇavādadhi saṃvatsaro ajāyata |"
    },
    {
      "n": 5,
      "refId": "RV10-190:5",
      "text": "Ordainer of the days nights, Lord over all who close the eye.",
      "original": "अहोरात्राणि विदधद्विश्वस्य मिषतो वशी",
      "translit": "ahorātrāṇi vidadhadviśvasya miṣato vaśī"
    },
    {
      "n": 6,
      "refId": "RV10-190:6",
      "text": "3. Dhatar, the great Creator, then formed in due order Sun and Moon.",
      "original": "सूर्याचन्द्रमसौ धाता यथापूर्वमकल्पयत् ।",
      "translit": "sūryācandramasau dhātā yathāpūrvamakalpayat |"
    },
    {
      "n": 7,
      "refId": "RV10-190:7",
      "text": "He formed in order Heaven and Earth, the regions of the air, and light.",
      "original": "दिवं च पृथिवीं चान्तरिक्षमथो स्वः",
      "translit": "divaṃ ca pṛthivīṃ cāntarikṣamatho svaḥ"
    }
  ]
}
